Subject: [PATCH 03918/11362] =?UTF-8?q?[outer-loop]=20DIAGNOSTIC:=20just-e?=
 =?UTF-8?q?xplore=20as=20primary=20on=20our=20offline=20harness=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20mechanism=20gap=20confirmed=20(gated)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Ran the cloned just-explore graph-exploration solver (3rd-place, CPU-only,
model-free, LLM-free) UNMODIFIED as the primary agent on our offline arcade (25
color-permuted public-game variants), at budget 200 (same as ours) and 2000
(raised), to decompose mechanism vs budget. Reproduction-gated apples-to-apples
with our 0.04 (all 13 solves PASS kit.reproduce under the correct JE label format):

  ours @200          : 0.04 (1/25)
  just-explore @200  : 0.16 (4/25)  -> MECHANISM delta +0.12 (4x better, SAME budget+gate)
  just-explore @2000 : 0.36 (9/25)  -> BUDGET delta +0.20

The 0.08 plateau is PRIMARILY a MECHANISM gap, not just budget/never-tried: a clean
graph-exploration explorer (frame-change edge enumeration + connected-component
segmentation + frontier BFS + per-level reset) is 4x better than our object-centroid
+ memory-dominated + goal-induction-first explorer at equal budget, and budget helps
further. (Caveat: PUBLIC games JE was tuned on; hidden-game transfer differs.)
Diagnostic measurement only -- NOT a submission; solve_provenance=development_proxy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
